 `priority` is optional (`normal`). Answers 201 with the new ticket, whose status is `open`. The requester is notified
 that the ticket was received.
 
+### Import tickets: `POST /tickets/import`
+
+For a move from another tracker. The body is a list of tickets, each as for `POST /tickets`, at most 5000 of them:
+
+```json
+{ "tickets": [
+  { "title": "VPN drops every hour", "requester": "maria@example.com", "priority": "high" },
+  { "title": "Printer jams", "requester": "li@example.com" }
+] }
+```
+
+Creates them in the given order, all of them, or none when any item is invalid: 400 `invalid`, and the message names the
+first invalid item by its index in the array (0 for the first). Answers 201 with how many were created and their ids:
+
+```json
+{ "created": 2, "ids": ["T-0001", "T-0002"] }
+```
+
+Each imported ticket is recorded and its requester is notified as when one ticket is created.
+
